        "original_id": "31c74724-9ed7-524d-812c-593914617f1f",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alexander Hall, Pierre Morel, Sidney Buchman, Seton I. Miller, Harry Segall\n- Works: Here Comes Mr. Jordan, Heaven Can Wait, Jhuk Gaya Aasman\n- Roles: film director, theatre actor, cinematographer, playwright\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander Hall was born on January 11, 1894, in Boston, Massachusetts, and he was an American film director and theatre actor.\n- Here Comes Mr. Jordan was released in 1941.\n- Here Comes Mr. Jordan was adapted by Sidney Buchman and Seton I. Miller from the play Heaven Can Wait.\n- Heaven Can Wait was written by Harry Segall.\n- Alexander Hall directed Here Comes Mr. Jordan.\n- Pierre Morel was born on May 12, 1964, and he is a French film director and cinematographer.\n- Alexander Hall died on July 30, 1968, in San Francisco, California.\n- Jhuk Gaya Aasman is a remake of the Hollywood film Here Comes Mr. Jordan.",
